title: Hotel Corridor
text: Four rooms, one door each onto the corridor, and the corridor leads nowhere. Both far rooms want both colours.
trick: each splitter at a door sends one colour the wrong way along the corridor; a mirror at each dead end sends it straight back, so the light returns through the other splitter's door and both rooms get red and blue
motif: rooms (a hotel corridor: four rooms, one door each)
expect: reversals>=2, merges>=1
